	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg8553"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Moderator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14333<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=788.msg8553#msg8553"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=788.msg8553#msg8553">Re: Laterz</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #55 on:</b> June 15, 2004, 03:03:34 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ya know, for the guy that admins this site, and was sorta pivotal, I let this whole thread slide right on by with little notice. It may be old news, but I hate inaccuracies.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Rough Timeline of the excitement:<br />1. Eelyen calls for this and that, but seldom shows up himself. Fignutn runs vast majority of FoT raids (maybe even all?)&nbsp; and his group is the only one even really trying to progress through Ikkinz trials. Eelyen gives them insights about these trials (holy trinity is not needed, which was posted after I said it was not needed on these boards), but remains unflagged even to Kod&#039;Taz. Some people are irritated by this whole high and mighty thing and the constant &quot;my&quot; rhetoric.<br /></div><br />Pretty sure Fig relayed that as it was. Fig did alot, no denying that. He was pretty active and all, working on getting people into Kod Taz. I&#039;ll admit, most other officers were getting pretty apathetic about the current state of the guild at that time.<br /><br />What was missed in this, Fig, and a few other people, some officers, some not asked me to be guild leader. Crazy as it was, this discussion came up like once back in December, and between two former officers they thought I&#039;d do ok as leader. My initial reaction was always &quot;WTF are you god damned crazy?&quot;<br /><br />I never wanted to be a guild leader to be blunt. If they hadn&#039;t have asked, I would have prolly walked away as well. But there were alot of people asking, and at that point, I figured I&#039;d go down fighting rather than walk away. Eelyen coulda just as easily told me to get the fuck outta dodge, and left it at that.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">2. Kinladar calls for a vote of no confidence in Eelyen<br /><br /><br />3. A vote for new guildleader is suggested and approved by the officers, and they start setting it up.<br /><br />4. Eelyen appears devastated and posts a sort of puppy eyed post about stepping down since he doesn&#039;t have the trust of HIS officers.<br /><br />5. Not surprisingly some members of the guild sympathize with him, since his martyrdom was fairly good. Basically some say the other officers are bit mean, which Eelyen takes to mean they think the other officers are wrong. They also feel Eelyen should run for leadership, since he does have significant backing still. Some people even guildremove (Deren).<br /><br />6. Eelyen rallies! The people are with him and he won&#039;t step down! He will run for leadership at the very least.<br /></div><br />Mostly accurate I suppose, if in an overly dramatic style.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">7. Core members including 4 of the 5 people (if I understand correctly) flagged through Ikkinz trials (unsure if Cyprian is actually flagged) get a deal from Triton to get full membership if they xfer, and they decide to xfer realizing they won&#039;t get rid of Eelyen that easily.<br /></div><br />The timing of this is a little out of sync with the rest, in that these people asked me to try and make a change, then barely 24 hours later have decided to server transfer after just a little time. <br /><br />Woulda been nice if they&#039;d have given it just a bit of time to sort things out, but I suppose I can&#039;t blame them. At the time it was pretty up in the air what the total result would be. <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">8. Eelyen goes for the motivational angle:<br />&quot;Inspiration for my guild.&quot;<br />&quot;I know this is a hard time. But be assured I refuse to let my guild fall. This was my dream and my vision when I started it nearly 2 years ago.&quot;<br /><br />9. &quot;my my my my my my my&quot; is the topic of the whole post, which annoys a great many people. It&#039;s the same old Eelyen. More than one poster scolds him for the stupid and self centered rhetoric.<br /></div><br />I can truthfully state that at this point Eelyen did really want to try and at least ensure the guild survived. I&#039;m sure that how I handled things kept this complicated for him as well, and was no easy thing to deal with.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">10. With much of the de facto authority of FoT now on Povar, Eelyen apparently believes he has enough support of those left, that an election is no longer necessary (even though the unofficial favourite Kinladar is still on RN, as are other prominent members such as Zenoflare).<br /></div><br />This is pretty inaccurate as a statment of fact. Fig was a very outspoken person in the guild and contributed a great deal, but I wouldn&#039;t have said that much of the defacto authority left for Povar. Certainly a good group of very skilled players, no denying that in any way shape or form. <br /><br />Fig was, and I know still is a great raid leader, always did a great job. But when it came to other things in regards to guild policies, I don&#039;t think he was very comfortable with alot of that. Or was just more focused on the here and now etc... Youth is good for that!<br /><br />I tended to be a bt quieter on the Raids, and did more from a standpoint of working with members, and listening to them.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">11. People that gave him sympathy originally scold him for this and hope he&#039;d let the election go ahead.<br /><br />12. Some ventrilo drama ensues, but we were busy in uqua and couldn&#039;t get very good real time commentary =(<br /></div><br />Hmm... mostly just that I misunderstand a great deal of what eelyen wanted to do in ventrilo. He was prepared to hand over guild leadership from his accounts as I found out after the fact, just wanted to set things in place to ensure the life of the guild as a whole.<br /><br />I think a part of me was still jaded, and not willing to listen. One of the few times I regret having such a hard headed view of things. But I was in take no prisoners mode by that stage, and just wanted it finished one way or the other.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">13. Eelyen realizes what he took for popular support was actually sympathy and respect (yes, respect, some might consider that surprising, but he has indeed done stuff for the guild in the past and deserves some for it).<br /><br />14. Eelyen decides to step down again.<br /><br />15. Guildleads are passed to Zenoflare.<br /><br /><br />This is the cliffhanger we were left at!<br /></div><br />To fill in these blanks, an open ballot is done, with Zenoflare, and myself as the only real nominees. Zeno opted not to accept his nomination. I did since obviously I am leader.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">That&#039;s the dramaish side. I left quite a bit out since it doesn&#039;t really reflect on the server that much.<br /><br />I feel it just shows how badly people handled things inside FoT. Eelyen obviously, but the palace revolution was also extremely clumsy IMHO. The goal of having a different leader than Eelyen might have been noble, since Eelyen indeed did not play enough... but it certainly came out badly to the members (you should have guessed Eelyen would do that).<br /></div><br />I won&#039;t deny I did things in a very brash manner, and certainly could have been handled differently. One of the reasons for what I did was based upon the actions of another officer, who tried to convince Eelyen to step down and give him leadership peacefully, all it did was cause bitterness, and distrust between them. <br /><br />After seeing this, and being asked to be guild leader, the only way to accomplish this in my mind was up front and direct. Perhaps too direct in this case. Part of it is just how I am. I had some other emotions flying around as well that just made me very anxious. I didn&#039;t want to see what the officer corps had accomplished over the last few months come to naught, and I knew that at least some were in the process of seeking new adventures. So direct, and quick action was needed in my mind.<br /><br />As it was, I failed to achieve part of my objectives. I did not retain that officer crew as a whole. But the positive side is that when I asked for help, looking for new officers, probably 2 dozen people stepped foward and wanted to help. Many of those are officers now.<br /><br />Some people still think that Fires of Time is just a drama ridden sack of shit guild, regardless of who may be leader etc...<br /><br />But for a bunch of people to be able to pull together, and not splinter apart after all this means there is alot more to this group of people than who the leader is. It&#039;s the reason I&#039;ll do my best for these people regardless of how my personal &quot;vision&quot; for what should have been came out, and what the reality is today.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Guild Leader of <a href="http://www.fotguild.com" target="_blank">Fires of Time</a><br /><br /><span style="font-family: 2;">A little piece of paper with a picture drawn<br />&nbsp;floats on down the street till the wind is gone. <br />The memory now is like the picture was then, <br />When the paper&#039;s crumpled up, it can&#039;t be perfect again. </span>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
